{"title":"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/9/ac992956a755ec5c20b8f39f663157112605bb9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)=kx^3 + 2k^2x^2+k^3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"21\" /> Find the sum of all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be4e0c9fe53284fc1fc418baf62e3a7253237ce7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/323088fb42c331a4aec675859f9e885c5b174f4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"46\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4d54250ec7584e4d21b9de6313c3f1ef39f7a09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) }-8 \\qquad \\text{(B) }-4 \\qquad \\text{(C) }0 \\qquad \\text{(D) }5 \\qquad \\text{(E) }8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"377\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Factor_Theorem\" title=\"Factor Theorem\"> factor theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be4e0c9fe53284fc1fc418baf62e3a7253237ce7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5a754da28ea41af23c9046c879ab274f3f20b5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2)=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/7/e4797950b5e812b65381cbc5fc33ad2db5f57aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ff1b9f95999ac571e17cd0baa8b1ddd67bba334.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(2)=0=2^3k+2(2^2)k^2+k^3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"248\" height=\"21\" /> which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d0413f154dda2eba54d5ca34a74540ddbb945c51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(k^2+8k+8)=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"155\" height=\"21\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/badf0ecd1ef8289387d8462393438c6e2710ff28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is a trivial real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/1/4d19902607daabb257bc4c315d712c0a219e9080.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8^2 -4(1)(8)=32 &gt; 0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"21\" /> this polynomial does indeed have two real zeros, meaning we can use Vieta’s Formula to conclude that sum of the other two roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812079b7d4364d1c6259885dd4bd4d6225879419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-8.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> \n</p><p>Thus, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/9/9f96f423815da67138cb1fbeb37bff193a270704.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0-8=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ -8}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"149\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P\">2002 AMC 10P</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Answer_Key\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_10\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2002_AMC_10P_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2002 AMC 10P Problems/Pro